    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_8fe4e16b",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image features a Black man with a serious expression against a textured background, overlaid with text that delivers a moralistic message about relationships and financial responsibility. The text advises against having multiple girlfriends, suggesting that it leads to financial loss and lack of life progress, and instead promotes finding one girlfriend to invest in and build a future together. While the message is framed as advice, it contains harmful stereotypes by implying that Black men are inherently prone to financial irresponsibility and relationship instability due to having multiple partners. This perpetuates a negative stereotype that links Black men with promiscuity and financial mismanagement, which is a form of racialized misogyny and harmful generalization. The meme uses the man's image to visually reinforce the stereotype, potentially reinforcing damaging societal narratives about Black men's behavior and financial competence. The overall intent is to deliver a moralistic, racially coded message that could be interpreted as a warning or judgment, which may contribute to harmful social perceptions and discrimination against Black men.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_460e5cdf"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_3c0af3cb",
      "@type": "TextualMaterial",
      "instance_name": "top_text",
      "label": "top text overlay",
      "description": "my brother, the more girlfriends you have the more money you lose, the more you don't progress in life",
